==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Corodragon & Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Corodragon is somewhat decent as a unit having fairly enough viability in the [[Into the Future]] chapter thanks to its massive damage ability, matching in similar strength to a maxed-out [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] when attacking Aliens. Its usage somewhat dwindles thanks to the addition of starred Aliens so keeping this unit away from enemies that can deal a mighty punch is important, especially when you're stacking this unit. Despite all this, Corodragon still maintains usage throughout Into the Future and [[Cats of the Cosmos]] in The Battle Cats Unite as additional backup thanks to its mid-range and stacking capabilities. Just like other Corocoro collaboration units, it has tremendously low XP costs and can easily help climb the user ranks.

When strategizing with this unit, it can be treated as powerful mid-ranger throughout the entirety of [[Empire of Cats]] as it is more accessible in terms of levelling up and costs in the main chapters. It's single target ability should be kept note of as it may keep it from progressing through troughs of peons when compared to [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], however you may have other attackers to help plow through the stage. Usage dwindles in the [[Legend Stages/SoL|Stories of Legends]] as Aliens have a lack of presence overall, leaving Corodragon with no outstanding niche. However, in the [[Heavenly Tower]] it can be used once more in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 5|Floor 5]], [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 17|Floor 17]], and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 23|Floor 23]].

