==Trivia==
*It, [[Kabuto Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]], [[Kuwagata Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kuwagata Cat]], [[Undies Cat Jr. (Switch Special Cat)|Undies Cat Jr.]], [[Manga Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Cat]], and [[Manga Boogie Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Manga Boogie Cat]] are exclusives specifically for The Battle Cats Unite JP Version, as serial codes do not work in the Southeast Asia version.
*Corodragon—as well as Kabuto Cat, Kuwagata Cat, and Cat Bros—initially did not have "+" levels, these were later changed in subsequent updates such as [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.4 Update|Patch 1.0.4]] for Cat Bros and [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]] for it, Kabuto Cat, and Kuwagata Cat.
*Corodragon has had the most amount of reruns in code distributions, these distribution events include: 「次世代ワールドホビーフェア'19 Winter」, Corocoro May 2019 issue, and Corocoro October 2023 issue.
*Corodragon's Normal Form's spritesheet contains a basic cat, however this goes unused in-game.

